## The task
Issue SAK-50842 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Gradebook: Accessibility - Set Score for Empty Cells not returned to focus after confirmation cancel
Area: Gradebook

When using the Gradebook item option “Set Score for Empty Cells” there is an initial modal to set the Grade Override and a confirmation dialog after clicking ”Done”l. If selecting Cancel or X in the confirmation dialog it closes but does not return focus to the modal. At that point there is no tabbing within the modal to allow a corrected value to be entered or outright cancelling of the action.

Additionally, when the confirmation dialog is opened it doesn’t have focus until mouse clicked into or tabbed into and if enter key is errantly pressed before establishing focus, the modal backdrop increasingly darkens each time enter is keyed.

Due to a different gradebook accessibility issue in 23.x, [+SAK-50757 - Gradebook: Modals launched from cell not receiving focus+|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-50757],  the demonstration video uses mouse click to get the “Set Score for Empty Cells” open to begin with.

Test Plan (in 23.x you will need to use mouse click instead of tabbing at certain points to due issue mention in SAK-50757)

