## The task
Issue SAK-51536 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Gradebook > Custom Export: Columns incorrect, data in wrong columns
Area: Gradebook

A fix was recently applied to 26x for exports if the GB had no GB items, only a Grade Override: [https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-50351|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-50351|smart-link] 

In testing further due to other issues, the columns are incorrect if there are GB items. Also, doing a Custom Export adds more columns to the export than asked for. There is a difference between 26x and 25x because the fix for SAK-50351 has not been merged yet, but both 26x and 25x are incorrect.

Tests need to be done with an empty GB, with only a course grade override, and then again with GB items added.

Options selected on both 26x and 25x:

!image-20250522-212428.png|width=639,height=739,alt="image-20250522-212428.png"!

26x has a “bogus” column “# This column will be ignored” if there are no GB items.

Once there are GB items, that column disappears and the course grades are in the Grade Override column and the actual grade override is in the following column with no heading.

!image-20250522-212541.png|width=1076,height=547,alt="image-20250522-212541.png"!

25x has example columns if there are no GB items, and the Grade Override is in the first example column.

Once GB items have been added, selecting the same options for Custom Export, now adds an additional column “# Student Number”, but the course grade and grade override values are in the correct columns.

!image-20250522-213031.png|width=779,height=397,alt="image-20250522-213031.png"!

