Title: Contact Us: Submit button  Uncaught TypeError: $.handleError is not a function
Area: Feedback Tool

This does not affect 23x. On 26 & 25, when trying to submit a Contact Us form for Problem with Content, Ask for help, or Report a technical problem, the Submit button doesn’t seem to do anything, (but the email actually does get sent). 

Hitting the Cancel button returns the user to the main Contact Us page and that is what I would expect to happen when the Submit button is clicked.

On 23x, once the user has submitted the form, the main Contact Us page displays with the following message:

An email with the information you entered has been sent to <instructor’s name> (site contact)

*Console error*:

{noformat}jquery.form-2.43.js:339 
 Uncaught TypeError: $.handleError is not a function
    at cb (jquery.form-2.43.js:339:7)
    at HTMLIFrameElement.onload (219760ec-7b4a-4264-9…9-b61d68474430:1:42)
{noformat}

!image-20250721-144247.png|width=826,height=572,alt="image-20250721-144247.png"!



*Co-pilot suggestions:*

Uncaught TypeError: $.handleError is not a function



means that the {{jquery.form-2.43.js}} script is trying to call a jQuery function named {{handleError}}, but that function does not exist or has not been defined when it’s being called.

This happens at line 339 in that script when the {{cb}} function executes—possibly during an {{iframe.onload}} event.

