Some auto-graded types do not generate a tally in Totals Scores view (arguably they should - see test plan). Non-Autograded question types do no generate a tally in Total Scores view. (this is to be expected).  However, when {color:#ff5630}*any of these above types are included*{color} in an assessment then Total Scores view’s column {color:#ff5630}*“Correct/Incorrect/Blank” is suppressed*{color} - {color:#ff5630}*even if other questions are which are normally supported such as True/False and some Multiple Choice . The presence of the error prone auto-graded type or non-autograded type suppress the column. That should be considered a major bug.*{color}

