## The task
Issue SAK-52230 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Syllabus: sanitizer warning blocks publish after AntiSamy strips align attribute
Area: Syllabus

When instructors paste HTML with disallowed attributes into a new syllabus item, AntiSamy cleans the markup but the JSF flow treats the warning as a blocking validation error. The page reloads and nothing is saved even though the content has already been sanitized.

* Example: adding a new item with <h1 style="font-style:italic" align="center">Sam Test</h2><p>1</p> shows a red error banner and Publish just reloads the page without saving. The align attribute is removed, but the
item is never persisted.
* Expected: AntiSamy should sanitize quietly and proceed with save/publish so instructors aren’t blocked or shown scary HTML errors.
* Fix implemented: treat AntiSamy warnings as informational; keep the sanitized content and continue the JSF flow instead of setting alertMessage/returning to edit. Log the sanitizer notes for admins.

