Issue SAK-52435 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Web Content: Importing from site does not transfer all props from source site
Area: Web Content

*Summary* 
When a Web Content tool is copied from a source site using “Import from Site” with “Copy Web Content” selected, certain tool properties are not carried over to the destination site. Most notably, the “Open in new window?” setting (popup) is lost. Other properties stored in the sakai_site_tool_property table (e.g., maximize, xframe-last-time) also do not transfer.



*Steps to Reproduce*

# In a source site:
#* Add a Web Content tool.
#* Edit the tool and enable “Open in new window?”.
# In a different (destination) site:
#* Use “Import from Site”.
#* Select the source site.
#* Check “Copy Web Content”.
#* Complete the import.
# After import:
#* Open the copied Web Content tool in the destination site.
#* Inspect its settings and relevant properties.

*Some properties are missing in the destination site.:*

The “Open in new window?” setting is not enabled after import.
Additional properties from sakai_site_tool_property (e.g., maximize, xframe-last-time) are not present

