## The task
Issue SAK-52629 (Bug, Verified, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Date Manager: bulk date setter should hide date fields that are not used by any tool in the site
Area: Date Manager

[https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-52523|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-52523|smart-link] introduced a new feature - bulk date setter controls.

The date manager only displays tools that are actually in the site, while the bulk date setter includes fields that are not used by any of the tools.

If a date field is not used, it should be hidden from the user so it does not cause extra confusion

Example 1: Only Gradebook, Resources and Announcements are in the site, so the only dates I would expect to see are Open and Due Date

!image-20260603-161306.png|width=671,alt="image-20260603-161306.png"!

Example 2: Adding assignments to the site now uses an “Accept Until Date”, so I would expect it to be included but not the Show/Hide Feedback dates or the Sign-up dates

!image-20260603-161502.png|width=671,alt="image-20260603-161502.png"!

