## The task
Issue SAK-52848 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: GradeBook/Date Manager - Gradebook due date becomes one day behind for UTC users when changed via Date Manager
Area: Date Manager, Gradebook

If your time zone is set to UTC and you create a Gradebook item with a due date, then go to Date Manager, the due date is reflected accurately. However, if you change the date in Date Manager, the due date in the Gradebook will show a date that is one day behind the date you set in Date Manager.



Here’s a video showing that behavior on 27x:

!27x Behavior.mov|width=727,alt="27x Behavior.mov"!



This issue also affects 25x. It affects 23x as well, but the behavior is slightly different: if you set the due date in Date Manager, the Gradebook shows a date one day behind (like 27x and 25x), but if you return to Date Manager, it will also show the same date as the Gradebook (one day behind the date you originally set in Date Manager). I have attached a video of the 23x behavior as well.

!23x Behavior.mov|width=727,alt="23x Behavior.mov"!

