## The task
Issue SAK-52862 (Feature Request, Resolved, Fixed, priority Minor)
Title: Statistics New Analytics: Presence and access
Area: Sitestats

Based on T&L's comments in ticket SAK-52659, we propose splitting the current *Visits* section into:

# *Visits*: Focused on traffic volume, unique user metrics, and trend over time.
## KPIs:
### Total visits (Numeric). The total number of times the site was accessed, including multiple visits by the same person.
### Users who have visited site (Numeric). The count of distinct individual accounts or visitors who logged at least one visit.
### Members who visited (Format: Count / Total Members + %). The number and percentage of officially enrolled site members who have accessed the site.
### Last visit (Date). Displays the exact timestamp/date of the most recent access to the site by a student.
### Traffic trend (last 7 days) (Format: Count + % change). The volume of visits over the past week compared to the previous 7-day period, showing percentage growth or decline.
## Visual Chart: Bar chart representing Visits (last 30 days).
## Accordion Breakdowns: By date, By user, and By role.
# *Presence and Access*: Focused on engagement metrics, bounce rate, and presence duration.
## KPIs:
### Median time on site (Format: X hrs. Y min. or X days). The midpoint duration of user sessions, providing a realistic estimate of average time spent without skewing from extreme outliers.
### Bounce rate (visits under 5 min) (Format: Count / Total Visits + %). The proportion of total visits that lasted less than 5 minutes, signaling low engagement or accidental clicks.
### Total presence (Durat
