## The task
Issue SAK-52877 (Bug, Verified, Fixed, priority Critical)
Title: T&Q Hot Spot scoring uses the marker's top-left instead of the student's click
Area: Tests & Quizzes (Samigo)

Hot Spot (image map) delivery stores the top-left of the on-screen pointer widget, not the pixel the student clicked.

On the evaluation screen the whole marker (crosshair + number) sits on the target, so the click looks correct. Scoring uses the corner of the marker, which sits up and left of the click.

In large areas, this usually has no significant impact. However, in small areas where the student needs to be quite precise, this error causes the student's pointer to fall outside the response area.

The student's answer:

!image-20260907-130614.png|width=487,alt="image-20260907-130614.png"!

What Sakai grades:

!image-20260907-130513.png|width=487,alt="image-20260907-130513.png"!

!image-20260907-130703.png|width=487,alt="image-20260907-130703.png"!

