- [user] Horner Thanks for testing that on the production clone!

The reason Case 1 maxed out your CPU is because running Case 2 first created ~190k new orphaned rows for Case 1 to process.

We definitely need to run *Case 1* (the {{DELETE}}) to clear out the existing data, but we should do it *without* running Case 2 first. Since there are only about 200 initial records for Case 1, it should run quickly on its own.

*Case 2* (the {{UPDATE}}) can safely be deferred to a later low-activity maintenance window, as it just flags the remaining redundant rows for a future cleanup.

