## The task
Issue SAK-51994 (Improvement, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Scorm logging improvements and clean up
Area: SCORM Player

There are many improvements that can be made to the code in scorm

  What was checked:

* Syntax errors: No missing newlines, malformed catch/else statements
* Logging consistency: All [user] annotations properly paired with imports
* Text blocks: Properly formatted multiline strings with correct termination
* Import statements: All static imports and regular imports are valid
* Annotation formatting: [user], [user], and other annotations correctly placed
* Bracket matching: No unclosed parentheses or braces
* String literals: No unterminated strings
* Consistent Lombok [user] usage across 95+ files
* Proper modern Java features (text blocks, parameterized logging)
* Clean migration from System.out.print to structured logging
* No deprecated logging patterns remaining

