Issue SAK-52171 (Bug, Open, priority Major)
Title: SCORM: Lag with the SCORM packages in player
Area: SCORM Player

The Quiz.zip file is really lagging when the student answers the questions and the Golf files sometimes take a long time to submit the quiz, and the lag is not dependent on the browser used. 

Quiz.zip: Articulate Storyline 360

Golf files are from [https://scorm.com/scorm-explained/technical-scorm/golf-examples/|https://scorm.com/scorm-explained/technical-scorm/golf-examples/|smart-link]

## Their verdict
- COMMENTED
- COMMENTED

## What they pointed at in the code
- scormplayer/scorm-tool/src/java/org/sakaiproject/scorm/ui/player/util/CompressingContentPackageResourceStream.java:72 — a static member cache is going to be visible by all threads, your going to need to think about how this is accessed and more importantly updated. There are better modern patterns than using synchronized collections. maybe COW, maybe Atomic I am not saying this is wrong but you need to think this through and understand your choices.
- scormplayer/scorm-tool/src/java/org/sakaiproject/scorm/ui/player/util/CompressingContentPackageResourceStream.java:72 — I did a little looking for you

This class is used here
```
	public IResourceStream getResourceStream()
	{
		if (canCompress())
		{
			return new CompressingContentPackageResourceStream(resource);
		}

		return resourceStream;
	}

```

Which means a new instance is created for each request, this is thread safe, by adding the static member variable your changing this and adding threading complexity to a class clearly not meant to be used this way. IMO if the cache is needed it should not live in this class.

