## The task
Issue SAK-52334 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Follow up to FormattedText sanitizing where messages are now going back to tools
Area: Global, Kernel

In [https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-51863|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-51863|smart-link] {{org.sakaiproject.util.impl.FormattedTextImpl#processFormattedText(java.lang.String, java.lang.StringBuilder, org.sakaiproject.util.api.FormattedText.Level, boolean, boolean, boolean)}}

the “return” config option was removed and supplying a StringBuilder for the messages will return any messages antisamy generated during text sanitizing. Because tools were never receiving this message people got used to not seeing these types of messages. I’ve updated the tools to reflect that.

If the messages are needed supply an instance of StringBuilder but if not needed pass a null which is essentially how it was working previously.

One thing to note was I removed some reflection code in lessons which was used to figure out if FormattedText service was available, it is always available these days so I removed the legacy code.

