## The task
Issue SAK-51160 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Fix the attachment upload modal
Area: Attachment Widget

From [https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-51102|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-51102|smart-link] : it is possible to upload an attachment now but the method is very clunky.

[user] comment from 51102:

{quote}There does seem to be a delay as the page reloads which is just long enough for the user to know that there is another page in the background before the modal appears. I think seeing that other page is what makes it feel awkward, since you have enough time to see something happening behind the modal but you can’t focus on it long enough to really see what it is (and if you do happen to get a glimpse, it is just a repeat of the information that appears in the modal, which seems a little redundant). Is there any way we could either speed up the refresh or hide the info on the screen behind the modal to show a blank page so the user doesn’t have time to catch a glimpse of it?  Maybe just increasing the size and location of the modal would be enough to hide what is behind it. I’m attaching a recording showing what I think is the problem. If the behavior of the current modal can’t be modified to hide that intermediary screen, then I think replacing it with the Lessons file upload behavior would be preferable.{quote}

Am attaching the video from Wilma in 51102.

