## The task
Issue SAK-52524 (Improvement, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: SCORM: if a student submits after the due date, but before the accept until date, the instructor should have some indicator that the student submitted late
Area: SCORM Player

If a SCORM package has a due date and an accept until date, before the due date it shows as “Open” to the student, after the due date but before the accept until date it shows as “Overdue” but the student can still launch the file, and once the accept until date has passed, it shows as “Closed” and can no longer be launched by the student. This is all working very well for the student.

If the student submits after the due date but before the accept until date, the instructor has no indicator that the submission was late. It would be good to have a “late” label applied as it is with assignments and Tests & Quizzes.

