## The task
Issue SAK-49219 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Critical)
Title: Conversations: Topic not locked when there is only a due date and no late date
Area: Conversations

If the instructor chooses to create a Conversation topic with a due date, but no late allowed date, the topic never locks and the student sees the following message (which is {color:#bf2600}*incorrect*{color}!) and can continue to post: 

Due date is passed, however late responses are accepted

When the instructor clicks Edit for the Conversation, you can see a Lock date was not set.

Compare this to due date with late accepted topics:

When the instructor sets a due date and a accepted late responses, the student sees the following message (which is correct):  Due date is passed, however late responses are accepted

After the accepted late date, students are not able to post anymore.

When the instructor clicks Edit for the Conversation, you can see a Lock date was set. 

*I would have expected a lock date to be automatically set for the due date/time when late responses are not accepted, and students should no longer be able to post.*

