## What they wrote in the discussion
- Upvoting is working, but it may not be working the way you expect. Duke had some particular views on how upvoting should be represented to the student. I’ve attached a screenshot of it working.
- I wasn’t trying to be patronising 🙂  It just is a bit weird around who can see how many upvotes there are. Duke didn’t want to leave any chance of students being shamed that their posts didn’t gain any traction.
- Maybe if nobody has the upvote permission, then we don’t show that toggle? Or we just do away with the toggle altogether? Or, we don’t have that permission and just use the toggle?

