## What they wrote in the discussion
- I understand that this is a change in behaviour from 22. However, the behaviour in 23 and 25 now fully respects the Sakai entity system, in that a folder in Sakai is an entity and has a unique reference and permissions map 1:1 onto references. I can change this is to reflect the <=22 behaviour but perhaps we may want to consider it for a moment? If a folder initially inherits the site’s permissions, but we allow instructors to override those in folders, is that a bad thing?
- Looking into this stuff, I find that when you click Permissions at the tool level (not on a folder or file) then the permissions loaded and applied to the site realm, *_not_* the top level site collection folder. Is this right? Shouldn’t the Permissions button at the top of the tool apply the permissions to the top level site collection?
- [user] Would you mind creating a new Jira for this latest regression? I’m finding it really hard to keep track of the user pathways. One thing that I did spot in the permissions rest controller is that if the requested realm is not available, the code returns the permissions for the *site*, not the top level folder, which is an omission on my part. Maybe it’s that.

