## The task
Issue SAK-51506 (Improvement, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Rubrics: a large number of public rubrics slows down the tool’s loading time
Area: Rubrics

In our production environment, we have around 300 public rubrics. With version 25, every time the tool is accessed, all of them are added to the DOM, which can take between 5 and 10 seconds, during which the tool is blocked and unusable.

## Their verdict
- CHANGES_REQUESTED: I've spotted a few things you should change. But, overall, what performance problems did you notice? Did you run Chome's performance analysis tools on the page. I find it very odd that a render of 300 public rubrics caused an issue in the actual UI code. Maybe the problem is server side? Or maybe it is network bound, like a bunch of fetches using up all the browser threads. I think we need more information about the need for this patch, personally.

