## The task
Issue SAK-50789 (Bug, Verified, Fixed, priority Blocker)
Title: Lessons improve import and feedback after import for LTI tools
Area: Lessons

Retesting [https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-49641|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/SAK-49641|smart-link] since there have been a lot of changes to LTI. I could only test 25x because 23x now gives an error “Uploaded file is larger than 20 MB”.

Last tested successfully:

* 7/21/24 - trunk
* 7/30/24 - 23x

When importing the python module into Lessons, it creates another link in the navigation. All the pages open in a new tab as expected except “Peer graded…” Clicking that link opens a form asking for a key/secret. Entering 12345 and secret deletes the entire module from Lessons and the navigation and places _Deleted_ text on the main Lessons page.

*From Chuck.*   This was broken with the refactor of the LTI data model.  But really, it was barely working before that.  The whole showing the key/secret page was a terrible workflow.  So I went through and cleaned this up a lot.  When you import a cartridge with an LTI link that does not match a pre-installed tool, it installs a stub tool (LTI 1.1 with dashes as secret and key).  If you go into the page, it will tee you further configuration is needed which can be done under Site Info → External tools.  See the test plan and screen shots.

