## The task
Issue SAK-50886 (Bug, Verified, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Calendar: should not import due dates since content imports in draft mode
Area: Calendar

The cc+ archive imports the Calendar and includes due dates for tools even though the content imports as drafts. Any events are created in the Calendar are fine to import, but the Calendar should not import due dates.

When the instructor actually publishes/posts the content, then the due dates should be added to the Calendar, not before, as it will cause instructors to have to do much cleanup.

The attached file contains 2 assignments with due dates, 1 quiz with a due date, 1 discussion topic with a due date and  1 conversations question with a due date.

All except for the Conversations Question import as drafts, but their due dates are on the Calendar. Conversations is currently not importing content, but the due date is posted to the Calendar.

Note: there is no sign-up event in the attached file, but that is another tool that posts dates to the Calendar and should not import the Calendar dates.

*Developer note:*  I added new data to exports to identify Assignment, Samigo, and Topic due dates.  But for imports created before this fix is applied, Assignments can be identified through metadata, Samigo and Topic events can be identified by looking at the description but Forums cannot be identified in the description.  For for an old export - it can ignore all but forums - but if you do a new export it should ignore Assignment, Samigo, Topics and Forums  – [user] 

*Developer Note:* This is a simple enough patch to perhaps go
