## The task
Issue SAK-52093 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: LTI: Adding a stealthed tool link to a site and checking "Add Site Link" does not work if the site ID hasn't also been added to the "Deploy" page
Area: LTI

If a stealthed LTI tool has been added by the admin, and the admin then wants to add a tool link to a site, the link does appear in the site, but it will give a message to the instructor/student that the External Tool is missing or improperly configured. This message will also display anywhere else that placement has been allowed when the instructor adds the tool, (Lessons, for example), until the site ID has been added to the deploy list. 

In order for the link to work, the site ID *must* also be added to the Deploy list on the External Tools page. Click the # beside the stealthed tool to get to the Deploy page.

One thing to note, is even if a tool does not have the navigation placement selected, as in the screenshot below, if the site ID is in the Deploy list and the admin adds the tool to a site using the Tool Links > Create Tool Link and checks the box “Add Site Link”, the tool *will* display in the navigation. 

Currently, to automatically the navigation link, it needs to be done through the Tool Links > Create Tool Link page. Otherwise, the instructor needs to go to Site Info > Manage Tools and add the navigation link themselves, (but they can only do that if the navigation placement is checked when the tool is initially set up).

*A message on the Tool Links page would be helpful so admins know they need to add the site ID in both places.*

!image-20251016-210719.png|width=530,alt="image-20251016-210719.png"!

Adding the link to a site:

!image-20251016-130748.png|wi
