## The task
Issue SAK-50581 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Calendar: Cannot remove a custom field
Area: Accessibility, Calendar

While testing WCAG [1.4.11|https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/non-text-contrast.html] on the Calendar Add/Edit Fields tab, I noticed two things:

# The “Remove selected fields” button doesn’t work and causes a console error (shown in attached image)
# The contrast between an enabled and a disabled “Remove?” box is very low (WCAG [1.4.11|https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/non-text-contrast.html]). This is confusing because on a fresh site, ALL of the fields on the Calendar Add/Edit Fields tab are disabled, so the “Remove?” box cannot be clicked for them, but there is no indication that they are disabled.

Tested on [https://trunk-mysql8.nightly.sakaiproject.org/|https://trunk-mysql8.nightly.sakaiproject.org/|smart-link] , build: b0d7bea2

