## The task
Issue SAK-51779 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Gradebook: Rubric modal too low, making controls inaccessible when grading
Area: Gradebook

When using a rubric to grade students in Gradebook, the modal for displaying the rubric displays near the bottom of the browser window in Sakai 25 & 26 (unlike Sakai 23 and before). This becomes problematic when beginning to grade, such that rubric controls become inaccessible via a mouse, unless the instructor resizes the browser window. Refer to the attached screencast, GradebookRubricBug-20250730.mp4.

Update: I’ve since realized that the Grade Rurbric modal is draggable via the modal header. That said, I surmise that this may not be intuited by all users, so it would be good to revise the current placement of this modal.

