## The task
Issue SAK-50633 (Bug, Verified, Fixed, priority Critical)
Title: T&Q SEB: With permissions set to allow uploading, the student is unable to upload a file for the file upload question
Area: Tests & Quizzes (Samigo)

I created a quiz with a file upload question and some other questions. I’m attaching the SEB config file used. Even though permissions were set to allow the user to upload files, when the student tried to upload a file for the upload file question, the SEB browser displayed a message:


{quote}Uploading files is not allowed in the current SEB settings.

Please report this to your exam provider.{quote}

I tested on Win11: Firefox, Edge and Chrome

See the documentation: [https://safeexambrowser.org/windows/win_usermanual_en.html#DownUploadsPane|https://safeexambrowser.org/windows/win_usermanual_en.html#DownUploadsPane|smart-link] 

Allow downloading and uploading files: Usually to be used with permitted third party applications for which you want to provide files to be downloaded. Uploading can only be blocked by SEB when the website is using standard form elements (this is a restriction of the used Firefox browser engine).

Allow user to select custom download / upload directory: With this option activated, SEB will bring up a simple dialog when download is starting. The user can then choose any folder from the local file system

!image-20241023-231702.png|width=688,height=426,alt="image-20241023-231702.png"!

