## The task
Issue SAK-50351 (Bug, Closed, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Gradebook: Custom export with no GB items results in extra columns, data in wrong columns
Area: Gradebook

If an instructor has a gradebook with no GB items, the custom export option is always including the gradebook items and comments, even if those items are not selected. If the instructor selects other options that would have data (ie Course Grade Overrides), that data is shown in the column it would be if the example gradebook items were not present. 

See the attached files for examples. In the class I exported from, there were no gradebook items, but two students had course grade overrides

NoItems = The default export - Student ID, Student Name, Gradebook Item Scores, Gradebook Item Comments

CourseGrade_Override = Student ID, Student Name, Course Grade, Grade Override

GradeOverrideOnly = Student ID, Student Name, Grade Override

Items_CourseGrade_Override = Student ID, Student Name, Gradebook Item Scores, Gradebook Item Comments, Course Grade, Grade Override



I assume that the example items are added to the export to help inexperienced instructors edit the export file for re-import. However, I would expect that the example items are present only when gradebook item scores or gradebook item comments are selected, but are not included in the export when those options are not selected. Regardless of whether these are selected or not, the course grade override data should appear in the correct column

